<div class="page">

  <div class="page-header">
    <div class="page-number">18</div>
    <div class="issue-info"><em>American Builder, July 1935.</em></div>
  </div>

  <div class="top-tagline">PLEASANT&nbsp;&nbsp;•&nbsp;&nbsp;COLORFUL&nbsp;&nbsp;•&nbsp;&nbsp;STURDY&nbsp;&nbsp;•&nbsp;&nbsp;ECONOMICAL</div>

  <div class="main-title">HOUSES <span class="of">of</span> STUCCO</div>

  <div class="body-text">
    <span class="dropcap">N</span><span class="smallcap-start">EW</span> homes are selling. Modernized homes are selling. And homes
    finished in attractive, eye-inviting stucco are well up in the <em>profitable</em>
    sales parade. &#9679; Stucco as it is made and applied under today's specifications (and
    did you know that much of it is now <em>factory-prepared?</em>) is a finish particularly fitted
    to home building&mdash;both for new construction and for modernizing. &#9679; First of all,
    portland cement stucco is a durable, strong finish&mdash;actually it is a thin wall of concrete,
    and is comparably permanent, weatherproof and fire-resistant. &#9679; Second, stucco is
    applied in any texture suited to the architectural design&mdash;floated to a smooth finish,
    troweled in various semi-smooth effects, tooled, stippled, spatter-dashed, rough torn,
    or treated in other pleasing ways. &#9679; Third, with a finish coat made with <em>white</em> portland
    cement, <em>any color</em> is available in stucco&mdash;from pure white, through pastel tints of
    cream and salmon and tan and pink, to rich warm yellows and browns and greens and
    other shades. &#9679; Durability, texture, color&mdash;these are selling points for stucco that
    help convince your prospects of a home's desirability&mdash;and that mean ready turnover
    and profit to you. Want the details? Write Universal Atlas Cement Co. (<em>United States
    Steel Corporation Subsidiary</em>), 208 South LaSalle Street, Chicago.
  </div>

